-- TESTS for row IL-04: every expected value comes from the SOURCE (a cell of Schedule J, a figure
-- in s 334, a limb of s 1) or from what the REGULATOR prints (the National Insurance Institute's
-- rate pages, fetched 2026-10-06; URLs and sha256 in nii-il04-published-figures.l4). Each was
-- worked out before the module was run, by a computation over the source's cells that does not
-- use this encoding. Where a figure is a SCENARIO value (a hypothetical index reading, a threshold
-- for a year not yet published), the fixture's name says so.
--
-- REPAIRED 2026-10-07 (NOTES.md, "Repair 2026-10-07"): three expected values changed, because the
-- enacted 2025 budget-year Law s 19(6) and s 21 answer fork F3 (column D's upper part begins at the
-- reduced collection threshold from 1 January 2026); each changed line says so. The assertions
-- added by the repair are in the last section, "Repair 2026-10-07".
--
-- Every assertion here is expected to be satisfied. The assertions that are expected to FAIL
-- (Schedule J's printed totals against its items, and the Institute's composite rates where the
-- items do not reach them) are in nii-il04-tests-expected-red.l4, with their exact count.

§ `Tests`

§§ `Branch lists, as s 335 gives them (s 335 is not in this row)`

-- Read from s 335 (source lines 3611-3619) for a resident aged 18 to retirement age. The
-- Institute's composite rates for each column (below) confirm the lists for the self-employed and
-- for those who are neither: the items of these branches sum exactly to the printed composites.
`all nine branches` MEANS
    LIST `maternity`, `children`, `work injury`, `accident injury`, `unemployment`
       , `employees' rights in insolvency proceedings`, `disability`, `long-term care`
       , `senior citizens and survivors`

-- s 335(e) and (f) exclude "a controlling shareholder in a closely-held company" from
-- unemployment and insolvency contributions.
`the branches of a controlling shareholder who is an employee` MEANS
    LIST `maternity`, `children`, `work injury`, `accident injury`, `disability`, `long-term care`
       , `senior citizens and survivors`

-- s 335(e) and (f) are for employees; the rest reach the self-employed.
`the branches of a self-employed person` MEANS
    LIST `maternity`, `children`, `work injury`, `accident injury`, `disability`, `long-term care`
       , `senior citizens and survivors`

-- Work injury for one who is neither is at rates the Minister sets (s 340(a)(2)), and (e)-(f)
-- are for employees.
`the branches of an insured person who is neither` MEANS
    LIST `maternity`, `children`, `accident injury`, `disability`, `long-term care`
       , `senior citizens and survivors`

-- s 342(c)(1) (source line 3661, row IL-05) lists the branches in which an employer deducts from
-- the wage: s 335(a), (d), (e), (g), (h) and (i).
`the branches with a deduction from the wage` MEANS
    LIST `maternity`, `accident injury`, `unemployment`, `disability`, `long-term care`
       , `senior citizens and survivors`

`the branches with no deduction from the wage` MEANS
    LIST `children`, `work injury`, `employees' rights in insolvency proceedings`

`the version for 2026` MEANS `Schedule J — the version for a contribution month in` 2026
`the version for 2027` MEANS `Schedule J — the version for a contribution month in` 2027
`the version for 2028` MEANS `Schedule J — the version for a contribution month in` 2028

§§ `Schedule J — which version governs which year`

#ASSERT (`the version for 2026`)'s `name` EQUALS "Schedule J, the temporary version for 2025-2026, as read in 2024-2027"
#ASSERT (`the version for 2027`)'s `name` EQUALS "Schedule J, the permanent version, as read in 2024-2027"
#ASSERT (`the version for 2028`)'s `name` EQUALS "Schedule J, the permanent version, as printed"
#ASSERT (`Schedule J — the version for a contribution month in` 2040)'s `name` EQUALS "Schedule J, the permanent version, as printed"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Schedule J — the version for a contribution month in` 2025 BECAUSE "Schedule J as it stood before 1 January 2026 is not in the deposited text"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Schedule J — the version for a contribution month in` 2011 BECAUSE "Schedule J as it stood before 1 January 2026 is not in the deposited text"

§§ `Schedule J — figures read back against the source cells`

-- Item 4, employee, above the threshold: printed 1.96, noted "2.06" for 2024-2027 (line 4723, 4741).
#ASSERT `the figure` `the version for 2026` `prints for` `work injury` `in` `column C, above the threshold, employee` EQUALS JUST 2.06
#ASSERT `the figure` `the version for 2027` `prints for` `work injury` `in` `column C, above the threshold, employee` EQUALS JUST 2.06
#ASSERT `the figure` `the version for 2028` `prints for` `work injury` `in` `column C, above the threshold, employee` EQUALS JUST 1.96
-- Item 4, employee, not above: temporary 0.60 (no note); permanent 0.37, noted "0.47" (line 4741).
#ASSERT `the figure` `the version for 2026` `prints for` `work injury` `in` `column C, not above the threshold, employee` EQUALS JUST 0.60
#ASSERT `the figure` `the version for 2027` `prints for` `work injury` `in` `column C, not above the threshold, employee` EQUALS JUST 0.47
#ASSERT `the figure` `the version for 2028` `prints for` `work injury` `in` `column C, not above the threshold, employee` EQUALS JUST 0.37
-- Maternity: item 1 for the employee, item 2 for those who are neither (lines 4720-4721).
#ASSERT `the figure` `the version for 2026` `prints for` `maternity` `in` `column C, above the threshold, employee` EQUALS JUST 1.40
#ASSERT `the figure` `the version for 2026` `prints for` `maternity` `in` `column C, above the threshold, neither` EQUALS JUST 0.16
#ASSERT `the figure` `the version for 2028` `prints for` `maternity` `in` `column C, not above the threshold, neither` EQUALS JUST 0.11
-- A dash: unemployment for the self-employed (line 4725).
#ASSERT `the figure` `the version for 2026` `prints for` `unemployment` `in` `column C, above the threshold, self-employed` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Senior citizens and survivors, the temporary and permanent figures that differ (lines 4729, 4747).
#ASSERT `the figure` `the version for 2026` `prints for` `senior citizens and survivors` `in` `column C, not above the threshold, employee` EQUALS JUST 2.22
#ASSERT `the figure` `the version for 2028` `prints for` `senior citizens and survivors` `in` `column C, not above the threshold, employee` EQUALS JUST 1.67
#ASSERT `the figure` `the version for 2026` `prints for` `senior citizens and survivors` `in` `column E` EQUALS JUST 0.25

-- Every version prints, for each branch and each figure column, a figure in at most one item
-- (maternity's two items never both print in one column). Checked over all nine branches and all
-- nine columns for each of the four versions.
`all nine figure columns` MEANS
    LIST `column C, above the threshold, employee`, `column C, above the threshold, self-employed`
       , `column C, above the threshold, neither`, `column C, not above the threshold, employee`
       , `column C, not above the threshold, self-employed`, `column C, not above the threshold, neither`
       , `column D, upper part of the wage`, `column D, part of the wage not above the threshold`, `column E`

GIVEN v IS A `A version of Schedule J`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`for every branch and figure column, at most one item prints a figure in` v MEANS
    all `for the branch` `all nine branches`
    WHERE
        `for the branch` b MEANS all (GIVEN c YIELD `at most one for` b c) `all nine figure columns`
        `at most one for` b c MEANS
            count (mapMaybe (GIVEN r YIELD `the cell of` r `in` c) (filter (GIVEN r YIELD r's `branch` EQUALS b) (v's `rows`))) AT MOST 1

#ASSERT `for every branch and figure column, at most one item prints a figure in` `Schedule J, the temporary version for 2025-2026, as printed`
#ASSERT `for every branch and figure column, at most one item prints a figure in` `Schedule J, the temporary version for 2025-2026, as read in 2024-2027`
#ASSERT `for every branch and figure column, at most one item prints a figure in` `Schedule J, the permanent version, as printed`
#ASSERT `for every branch and figure column, at most one item prints a figure in` `Schedule J, the permanent version, as read in 2024-2027`

-- Column D prints a figure exactly for the branches in which s 342(c)(1) makes the employer
-- deduct, and "–" for the others (a cross-check of the schedule against source line 3661).
GIVEN v IS A `A version of Schedule J`
      c IS A `A figure column of Schedule J`
      b IS A `A branch of insurance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the version` v `prints a figure in` c `for` b MEANS
    NOT (`the figure` v `prints for` b `in` c EQUALS NOTHING)

#ASSERT all (GIVEN b YIELD `the version` `the version for 2026` `prints a figure in` `column D, upper part of the wage` `for` b) `the branches with a deduction from the wage`
#ASSERT all (GIVEN b YIELD `the version` `the version for 2026` `prints a figure in` `column D, part of the wage not above the threshold` `for` b) `the branches with a deduction from the wage`
#ASSERT NOT (any (GIVEN b YIELD `the version` `the version for 2026` `prints a figure in` `column D, upper part of the wage` `for` b) `the branches with no deduction from the wage`)
#ASSERT all (GIVEN b YIELD `the version` `the version for 2028` `prints a figure in` `column D, upper part of the wage` `for` b) `the branches with a deduction from the wage`
#ASSERT NOT (any (GIVEN b YIELD `the version` `the version for 2028` `prints a figure in` `column D, part of the wage not above the threshold` `for` b) `the branches with no deduction from the wage`)

§§ `Schedule J — the National Insurance Institute's composite rates for 2026, column by column`

-- The Institute's rate pages (fetched 2026-10-06) print, for contributions from 01.01.2026 with
-- the reduced collection threshold at 7,703:
--   employees (18 to retirement age): National Insurance 5.55% up to the threshold (employer
--     4.51, employee 1.04), employee's share 1.04%;
--   a controlling shareholder in a closely-held company ("column 2" of form 102): total with
--     health insurance 8.71% up to the threshold, of which the employee 4.25%; health insurance
--     on employees is 3.23% up to the threshold, so National Insurance alone is 5.48%, and the
--     employee's National Insurance 1.02%;
--   the self-employed (18 to retirement age): 4.47% up to the threshold, 12.83% above;
--   the self-employed under 18 or receiving an old-age pension: 0.26% and 0.78%, "National
--     Insurance only" (the work-injury branch);
--   those who are neither, on income other than from work: 6.92% and 7%.
-- The composites above the threshold for employees are in the expected-red module.
#ASSERT `the combined percentage in column C of` `the version for 2026` `for` `an employee` `,` `the part not above the reduced collection threshold` `,` `in the branches` `all nine branches` EQUALS 5.55
#ASSERT `the combined percentage in column C of` `the version for 2026` `for` `an employee` `,` `the part not above the reduced collection threshold` `,` `in the branches` `the branches of a controlling shareholder who is an employee` EQUALS 5.48
#ASSERT `the combined percentage in column C of` `the version for 2026` `for` `a self-employed person` `,` `the part not above the reduced collection threshold` `,` `in the branches` `the branches of a self-employed person` EQUALS 4.47
#ASSERT `the combined percentage in column C of` `the version for 2026` `for` `a self-employed person` `,` `the part above the reduced collection threshold` `,` `in the branches` `the branches of a self-employed person` EQUALS 12.83
#ASSERT `the combined percentage in column C of` `the version for 2026` `for` `a self-employed person` `,` `the part not above the reduced collection threshold` `,` `in the branches` (LIST `work injury`) EQUALS 0.26
#ASSERT `the combined percentage in column C of` `the version for 2026` `for` `a self-employed person` `,` `the part above the reduced collection threshold` `,` `in the branches` (LIST `work injury`) EQUALS 0.78
#ASSERT `the combined percentage in column C of` `the version for 2026` `for` `an insured person who is neither an employee nor self-employed` `,` `the part not above the reduced collection threshold` `,` `in the branches` `the branches of an insured person who is neither` EQUALS 6.92
#ASSERT `the combined percentage in column C of` `the version for 2026` `for` `an insured person who is neither an employee nor self-employed` `,` `the part above the reduced collection threshold` `,` `in the branches` `the branches of an insured person who is neither` EQUALS 7.00

-- The employee's deduction (column D) on the part up to the threshold: 1.04%, and 1.02% for a
-- controlling shareholder (no unemployment).
GIVEN v IS A `A version of Schedule J`
      c IS A `A figure column of Schedule J`
      bs IS A LIST OF `A branch of insurance`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the combined column D percentage of` v `in` c `for` bs MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN b YIELD `the percentage in column D of` v `for` b `in` c) bs)

#ASSERT `the combined column D percentage of` `the version for 2026` `in` `column D, part of the wage not above the threshold` `for` `the branches with a deduction from the wage` EQUALS 1.04
#ASSERT `the combined column D percentage of` `the version for 2026` `in` `column D, part of the wage not above the threshold` `for` (LIST `maternity`, `accident injury`, `disability`, `long-term care`, `senior citizens and survivors`) EQUALS 1.02

§§ `Schedule J, column C, applied — the parts above and not above the threshold`

#ASSERT `the part of` 10000 `not above the threshold` 7703 EQUALS 7703
#ASSERT `the part of` 10000 `above the threshold` 7703 EQUALS 2297
#ASSERT `the part of` 7703 `above the threshold` 7703 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the part of` 5000 `not above the threshold` 7703 EQUALS 5000

-- A dash declines; work injury for one who is neither declines with s 340(a)(2)'s reason.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the percentage in column C of` `the version for 2026` `for` `unemployment` `,` `a self-employed person` `,` `the part above the reduced collection threshold` BECAUSE "Schedule J prints no rate for this branch in this column"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the percentage in column C of` `the version for 2026` `for` `work injury` `,` `an insured person who is neither an employee nor self-employed` `,` `the part above the reduced collection threshold` BECAUSE "work-injury contributions of an insured person who is neither employee nor self-employed are at rates the Minister sets under section 340(a)(2), not encoded here"

§§ `Section 337(a)(1) — an employee's monthly contributions`

GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the branches` IS A LIST OF `A branch of insurance`
      `the income` IS A NUMBER
      `s 341` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 343` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `An employee's month of contributions`
`an employee's month in` `the year` `paying` `the branches` `on` `the income` `with section 341 reduced rates:` `s 341` `and section 343 reduced work-injury contributions:` `s 343` MEANS
    `An employee's month of contributions` WITH
        `calendar year of the month`                                     IS `the year`
        `branches for which contributions are payable under section 335` IS `the branches`
        `monthly income on which contributions are computed`             IS `the income`
        `reduced rates under an order made under section 341 apply to this income` IS `s 341`
        `the employer pays reduced work-injury contributions under section 343` IS `s 343`

-- The ordinary case: neither s 341 nor s 343 reaches it.
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the branches` IS A LIST OF `A branch of insurance`
      `the income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `An employee's month of contributions`
`an employee's month in` `the year` `paying` `the branches` `on` `the income` MEANS
    `an employee's month in` `the year` `paying` `the branches` `on` `the income` `with section 341 reduced rates:` FALSE `and section 343 reduced work-injury contributions:` FALSE

