§§ `Section 337(a)(2) — another insured person`

GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the column` IS A `The Schedule J column of an insured person who is not an employee`
      `the branches` IS A LIST OF `A branch of insurance`
      `the annual income` IS A NUMBER
      `the periods` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Another insured person's year of contributions`
`another insured person's year` `the year` `in` `the column` `paying` `the branches` `on` `the annual income` `over` `the periods` MEANS
    `Another insured person's year of contributions` WITH
        `calendar year`                                                  IS `the year`
        `column`                                                         IS `the column`
        `branches for which contributions are payable under section 335` IS `the branches`
        `annual income on which contributions are computed`              IS `the annual income`
        `number of periods set for paying advances`                      IS `the periods`
        `reduced rates under an order made under section 341 apply to this income` IS FALSE

-- THE INSTITUTE'S WORKED EXAMPLE (page for those who are neither, fetched 2026-10-06): "in
-- January 2026, taxable rental income of 12,000 NIS and no other income": 3,442 is exempt (a
-- provision outside this row), leaving 8,558; "on the part up to 7,703: 12.09%, i.e. 931.29";
-- "on the remaining 855: 12.17%, i.e. 104.05"; "in total ... 1,035 NIS a month". 12.09% and
-- 12.17% include health insurance at 5.17% (same page). So National Insurance alone, at 6.92%
-- and 7%: 7,703 × 6.92% + 855 × 7% = 533.0476 + 59.85 = 592.8976.
`the Institute's example, as a year of 8,558 a month` MEANS
    `another insured person's year` 2026 `in` `the column for an insured person who is neither an employee nor self-employed` `paying` `the branches of an insured person who is neither` `on` (8558 TIMES 12) `over` 12

`health insurance at 5.17%, as the Institute's page prints it` MEANS 5.17%

#ASSERT `s 337(a)(2) — the contributions for each advance period, for` `the Institute's example, as a year of 8,558 a month` EQUALS 592.8976
#ASSERT FLOOR (`s 337(a)(2) — the contributions for each advance period, for` `the Institute's example, as a year of 8,558 a month` PLUS 8558 TIMES `health insurance at 5.17%, as the Institute's page prints it`) EQUALS 1035
-- The two slices, each against the Institute's printed figure to the agora.
#ASSERT TRUNC (`the contributions under` `the version for 2026` `for` `an insured person who is neither an employee nor self-employed` `on` 7703 `with the threshold at` 7703 `in the branches` `the branches of an insured person who is neither` PLUS 7703 TIMES `health insurance at 5.17%, as the Institute's page prints it`) 2 EQUALS 931.29
#ASSERT TRUNC (855 TIMES 7.00% PLUS 855 TIMES `health insurance at 5.17%, as the Institute's page prints it`) 2 EQUALS 104.05

