#ASSERT REFUSED `s 334(a)(1) — the threshold on 1 January of` 2029 `from` 8000 `by the index from` 100 `to` 105 BECAUSE "section 334(a)(1) updates the threshold by the index only on 1 January 2026, 2027 and 2028"
-- (2): the average wage rises 5% (10,000 to 10,500); 8,000 becomes 8,400.
#ASSERT `s 334(a)(2) — the threshold on 1 January of` 2029 `from` 8000 `by the average wage from` 10000 `to` 10500 EQUALS 8400
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 334(a)(2) — the threshold on 1 January of` 2028 `from` 8000 `by the average wage from` 10000 `to` 10500 BECAUSE "section 334(a)(2) updates the threshold by the average wage only from 1 January 2029"
-- A fall is applied as the formula gives it (fork F6): index 100 to 99, 8,000 to 7,920.
-- SUPERSEDED in version 0.4.0: fork F6 is a switch, declining by default (Meng, 2026-10-07,
-- TRIDENT). The assertion below now names reading (i), `the fall is applied`; its value is
-- unchanged: rate of rise (99 − 100) / 100 = −0.01, and 8,000 + 8,000 × −0.01 = 7,920.
#ASSERT `s 334(a)(1) — the threshold on 1 January of` 2027 `from` 8000 `by the index from` 100 `to` 99 `, reading a fall as` `the fall is applied` EQUALS 7920

-- Version 0.4.0: fork F6, a switch (NOTES.md, Version 0.4.0). s 334(a)(1)-(2), source lines
-- 3606-3607, update "by the rate of rise" (עליית) of the index or the average wage, and say nothing
-- of a fall. Ruled by Meng on 2026-10-07 (TRIDENT): declined by default.
#ASSERT `section 334(a) — the reading this row takes where the index or the average wage falls` EQUALS `a fall is declined`
-- The index falls, 100 to 99, from 8,000 in 2027.
--   (ii) the threshold stays where it was: 8,000.
#ASSERT `s 334(a)(1) — the threshold on 1 January of` 2027 `from` 8000 `by the index from` 100 `to` 99 `, reading a fall as` `the threshold stays where it was` EQUALS 8000
--   (iii) declined, and so by default.
