`the employee rate of a person aged 67 to 70 without an old-age pension, up to the threshold, with health insurance, as the Institute's page prints it` MEANS 3.93
`the employee rate of a person aged 67 to 70 without an old-age pension, above the threshold, with health insurance, as the Institute's page prints it` MEANS 10.03

-- The column D branches each pays (s 335, source lines 3611-3619). A controlling shareholder: all
-- but unemployment (s 335(e)). Aged 67 to 70 without an old-age pension: past retirement age, not
